{
    "background_story": "Calum was a gentle soul with a passion for botany. He spent most of his days tending to the gardens at the local estate, where he had a special fondness for the delicate muscari flowers. Their tiny, bell-shaped blooms reminded him of the blue skies of his childhood. As the seasons changed, Calum would carefully nurture the muscari, coaxing them to bloom in vibrant hues of blue and white. His love for these flowers was contagious, and soon the estate's gardens became a popular destination for nature lovers. Calum's kindness and dedication earned him the nickname 'The Muscari Whisperer.' As he worked among the flowers, he would often share stories of their symbolism \u2013 representing constancy and humility \u2013 values that Calum embodied in his own quiet, unassuming way.",
